> I'm not sure why I didn't include "group" and "replicate" in the inla.mesh.projector() interface when
> I wrote it; A clear oversight, and another item to put on my TODO list...

Replying to my own question: Some of this old original mesh/spde code is a bit counterintuitive when you start looking at the internals...
one would think that inla.mesh.project/or would be a "user friendly" interface to the raw basis function evaluations, that would be done by the more "maths heavy" inla.spde.make.A() interface.  In reality, it's the opposite; inla.spde.make.A() is a wrapper around the low level function inla.mesh.projector(), extending it to support replicates and groups, etc.  A new interface design would fix this more easily, but one could probably make the current interface a bit "smoother" in this respect still...

We have a draft version of a wrapper package that encapsulates all the A-matrix and stack stuff so the user won't have to deal with it directly, making these things a lot easier.  We hope to make it available for beta-testing soon(ish).

Finn

