> > > example that I could try with which you have tested that providing
> > > initial values of 'x' reduces the time required to fit the model? I
> > > am running INLA on Mac OS X and it also seems not to use multiple
> > > threads in the computations.
> > >
> >
> > I do not think there is a good example (or I do not have one at hand),
> > as this part converges quite quickly and is not that expensive in any
> > case. maybe if you go for int.strategy="eb" which will make the optim
> > step of the same order as the integration, but its a bit artificial.
